# Two GitHub accounts, one person. saxux2 is the canonical identity so that
# `git shortlog -sne` reports a single contributor rather than splitting the
# history across both addresses.
#
# Note that .mailmap only affects git's own output. GitHub credits the
# contribution graph from the raw author email, so commits authored as
# funnypost00 stay credited to that account there regardless of this file.
#
# The second entry uses the address-only form, `<canonical> <old>`, which
# rewrites both the name and the address for every commit under the old
# address. The name-qualified form would not: it matches on the recorded
# author name, and the previous entry here named a spelling those commits
# were never authored under.
saxux2 <skybiswas0722@gmail.com>
saxux2 <skybiswas0722@gmail.com> <funnypost00@gmail.com>
